1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,800
Welcome to SafeDeal on Avalanche Fuji C-Chain (43113).
Step 1: Passwordless Sign-In with Ethereum (EIP-4361) & CSRF session protection via OKX Wallet.

2
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:24,760
Step 2 [Happy Path]: Seller creates a new on-chain escrow.
Delivery terms are canonically hashed via RFC 8785, anchored via createTrade(), and verified by the Rust backend.

3
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:43,530
Step 3 [Happy Path]: Buyer verifies the SHA-256 RFC 8785 termsHash byte-for-byte in the browser,
then locks 0.01 AVAX into the non-custodial SafeDealEscrow vault via fundTrade().

4
00:00:50,350 --> 00:01:01,850
Step 4 [Happy Path]: Seller completes the work and signs markDelivered() on-chain,
transitioning the deal to DELIVERED and opening the 72-hour inspection window.

5
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:20,830
Step 5 [Happy Path]: Buyer inspects the work and signs releaseFunds() on-chain.
The deal transitions to RELEASED and credits 0.01 AVAX to the seller's pull-payment balance.

6
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:43,380
Step 6 [Pull-Payment Security]: Seller actively calls withdraw() on-chain to claim 0.01 AVAX,
eliminating reentrancy and reverting-contract DoS attacks.

7
00:01:46,500 --> 00:02:04,690
Step 7 [Dispute Path]: Buyer triggers openDispute() on-chain and uploads SHA-256 verified evidence,
protected by 2-of-3 multi-party consensus and a 14-day anti-lockup fallback.

8
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:41,270
Step 8 [2-of-3 Consensus Resolution]: UI enforces 100% payout integrity. Seller proposes a 50/50 split (0.005 AVAX each),
Buyer co-signs (2/3 votes), and SafeDealEscrow resolves the dispute on Avalanche!
